question:
Answer the following math problem in a strict structured format.

[Problem]
Regular octagon $ABCDEFGH$ has its center at $J$.  Each of the vertices and the center are to be associated with one of the digits $1$ through $9$, with each digit used once, in such a way that the sums of the numbers on the lines $AJE$, $BJF$, $CJG$, and $DJH$ are all equal.  In how many ways can this be done?
[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,J;
A=(20,20(2+sqrt(2)));
B=(20(1+sqrt(2)),20(2+sqrt(2)));
C=(20(2+sqrt(2)),20(1+sqrt(2)));
D=(20(2+sqrt(2)),20);
E=(20(1+sqrt(2)),0);
F=(20,0);
G=(0,20);
H=(0,20(1+sqrt(2)));
J=(10(2+sqrt(2)),10(2+sqrt(2)));
draw(A--B);
draw(B--C);
draw(C--D);
draw(D--E);
draw(E--F);
draw(F--G);
draw(G--H);
draw(H--A);
dot(A);
dot(B);
dot(C);
dot(D);
dot(E);
dot(F);
dot(G);
dot(H);
dot(J);
label("$A$",A,NNW);
label("$B$",B,NNE);
label("$C$",C,ENE);
label("$D$",D,ESE);
label("$E$",E,SSE);
label("$F$",F,SSW);
label("$G$",G,WSW);
label("$H$",H,WNW);
label("$J$",J,SE);
size(4cm);
[/asy]

